License: GPL-3
Comment: Ferrofin is derived from the Jellyfin media server
 (https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin), which it was written against as a
 reference. It is an independent project, not affiliated with, endorsed by
 or supported by the Jellyfin project.
 .
 /usr/bin/ferrofin-server statically links third-party Rust crates and C
 libraries, which keep their own permissive licenses (among them MIT,
 Apache-2.0, BSD and ISC); SQLite is public domain and jemalloc is
 BSD-2-Clause. libjpeg-turbo is under the IJG, BSD-3-Clause and Zlib
 licenses: this software is based in part on the work of the Independent
 JPEG Group, and libjpeg-turbo's Modified BSD License, which its TurboJPEG
 API asks binary distributions to reproduce, is the libjpeg-turbo-BSD-3-Clause
 paragraph below.

